Lower priority
The category route still imports INITIAL_CATEGORIES and INITIAL_LOCATIONS to start a listing query before the database-backed category and location information is resolved.

If the static initial data does not match the database-backed result, the first query can be wasted and another query can be issued.

This is not a correctness problem in the normal matching case.

It is an opportunity to avoid unnecessary database work.

I would address it after the major listing-cache work.

