Final verdict
The previous audit's central conclusion remains correct: the shared public listing-result cache is still missing. The current source is at the same commit I checked in the previous audit, so I found no newer commit containing additional fixes.

This deeper pass also uncovered two issues worth treating seriously before implementing more caching:
1. The last-known-good fallback can return stale category counts when the real result is zero.
2. The successful outbox-recording path can mark a newer pending invalidation as completed.
I would fix those before building the larger listing cache. Otherwise, you risk making the site faster while making its data freshness less reliable.

I have not changed your GitHub repository. I can prepare one tightly scoped Gemini prompt for Phase 1, with exact requirements and verification instructions, while explicitly prohibiting unrelated refactors or changes to website behavior.